<TD ALIGN="left" VALIGN="top"><FONT STYLE="font-family:Times New Roman" SIZE="2">The second part of the incentive fee, which we refer to as the incentive fee on capital gains during operations, is an incentive fee on capital gains earned on
liquidated investments from the portfolio during operations prior to a liquidation of the Company and is determined and payable in arrears as of the end of each calendar year (or upon termination of the investment advisory and administrative
